WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.066 --> 00:00:05.366
Professor Sycamore’s Pokémon summer camp

2
00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:09.566
is roaring along at a fever pitch and our heroes are in the thick of it!

3
00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:12.333
With each event, teams compete for points.

4
00:00:12.399 --> 00:00:16.566
The team with the most points will enter the Pokémon summer camp hall of fame,

5
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:19.033
as the Champion Diantha once did!

6
00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:22.633
Now, stay tuned as the battle for points heats up!

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.933
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.666
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

9
00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:33.233
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

10
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.300
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

12
00:00:39.366 --> 00:00:42.233
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

13
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

14
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

15
00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:50.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

16
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:54.333
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

17
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.533
- Fenn!
- Pika!

18
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.766
Then what happened next?

19
00:01:14.733 --> 00:01:16.566
Good evening, Trainers!

20
00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:20.333
- Is everyone having a good time at camp?
- Yeah!

21
00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:22.966
That’s marvelous to hear. Thanks!

22
00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:25.433
But I just happen to have an event planned for tomorrow

23
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.766
that’s even more marvelous.

24
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.000
- Wonder what.
- Pika!

25
00:01:29.066 --> 00:01:32.899
So, get ready for a favorite annual tradition at summer camp.

26
00:01:32.966 --> 00:01:35.433
It's Pokémon Orienteering!

27
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.199
Huh? Pokémon Orienteering?

28
00:01:38.266 --> 00:01:41.033
You see, the object of the race is for all teams

29
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.300
to get their cards stamped at every checkpoint,

30
00:01:43.366 --> 00:01:45.600
as they quickly make their way toward the finish line.

31
00:01:45.666 --> 00:01:47.733
The team in third place gets three points,

32
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.699
second place gets seven points and the first place gets ten.

33
00:01:52.199 --> 00:01:55.399
Team Froakie and Team Squirtle are tied with 13 points each.

34
00:01:55.466 --> 00:01:57.933
But all teams still have a chance to win,

35
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.800
so go out and do your best and, above all, have lots of fun!

36
00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:05.300
All right! Team Squirtle already claims those ten points!

37
00:02:05.366 --> 00:02:08.733
Oh, yeah? Those ten points are going to belong to Team Froakie!

38
00:02:08.799 --> 00:02:11.100
- Right, buddy?
- Pika! Pika!

39
00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:14.400
- Hey, Ash, how’s your foot feeling?
- Good as new!

40
00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:17.900
If we win, we’ll be in the lead with 23 points!

41
00:02:17.966 --> 00:02:20.866
Well, you’re going to have to beat us to do it!

42
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:24.600
Looking at the facts with a cool head, there’s no way we’re going to lose this!

43
00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:27.400
My analysis of the facts tells me we’re going to win!

44
00:02:27.466 --> 00:02:30.900
Hm!

45
00:02:30.966 --> 00:02:34.733
Well, it looks like everyone’s really motivated.

46
00:02:34.799 --> 00:02:37.066
Well, it’s show time.

47
00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:40.266
Listen up! They’re having Pokémon Orienteering tomorrow

48
00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:42.866
and all teams will be split up racing around the mountain

49
00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:45.766
and that will be the perfect time to grab their Pokémon!

50
00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:49.000
Unfortunately, our work won’t allow us to get away.

51
00:02:49.066 --> 00:02:51.766
They go for our grub so much, they’re licking the plates clean!

52
00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:55.266
- Will you snap out of it?
- Excellent cuisine!

53
00:02:55.333 --> 00:02:59.666
I applaud the three of you on your impeccable talent and work ethic!

54
00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:01.033
Thank you, ma’am!

55
00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.500
You’ve earned yourselves another nice bonus for the day,

56
00:03:03.566 --> 00:03:05.033
so keep up the good work!

57
00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.400
Yes, ma’am!

58
00:03:07.466 --> 00:03:11.166
Hm! We can grab their Pokémon later.

59
00:03:11.233 --> 00:03:13.766
Right now, business is greater than great!

60
00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:16.333
Time for some elbow grease!

61
00:03:16.399 --> 00:03:19.966
Rub-a-dub-dub. Team Rocket makes yummy grub!

62
00:03:31.266 --> 00:03:33.033
Good morning to you, everyone!

63
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:36.533
It’s time to begin day five with some Pokémon Orienteering,

64
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:40.533
a chance to combine your best efforts with team cooperation.

65
00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.399
We’re going to win those ten points for sure!

66
00:03:43.466 --> 00:03:44.566
Pika, Pika!

67
00:03:44.633 --> 00:03:47.166
- Right! There’s no doubt!
- Same for us!

68
00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:50.166
And we’ll come out the clear winners after today!

69
00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:53.000
Let’s go! All for one and one for all!

70
00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.166
Yeah!

71
00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:58.299
All right! Team Squirtle’s headed for the top of the mountain!

72
00:03:58.366 --> 00:04:00.233
- Ready?
- Yeah!

73
00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:02.733
All right then, on your mark!

74
00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:04.433
Hm!

75
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.933
Get set!

76
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.899
And go!

77
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.633
Everybody at your stations?

78
00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.399
Checkpoint A, reporting in.

79
00:04:20.466 --> 00:04:22.633
This is checkpoint B, all ready to go!

80
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.366
I’ll be able to monitor all teams from here during the race.

81
00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:29.000
I’ll be able to observe the Trainers carefully

82
00:04:29.066 --> 00:04:30.900
to see if they work together well

83
00:04:30.966 --> 00:04:34.533
and see how strong the bonds are with their Pokémon.

84
00:04:36.166 --> 00:04:40.266
This is Checkpoint A reporting in. The first team is approaching!

85
00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:43.700
I can already see a checkpoint! We’re there first!

86
00:04:43.766 --> 00:04:45.766
Come on guys, let’s move it!

87
00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:48.599
Whoever gets all the stamps first is what counts!

88
00:04:49.766 --> 00:04:50.766
Huh?

89
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:53.266
According to the map, the checkpoint should be

90
00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:55.099
around here somewhere, but where?

91
00:04:55.166 --> 00:04:59.066
- Hey, I sure don’t see any stamp booth.
- Pika!

92
00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.133
Everyone! Up here!

93
00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.133
- Hey! It’s Sophie!
- All the way up there?

94
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.966
Please send one Trainer from your teams up here along with their Pokémon

95
00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.300
and I’ll give you your stamp.

96
00:05:09.366 --> 00:05:11.833
We have to climb all the way up there?

97
00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.566
That’s a bit extreme.

98
00:05:13.633 --> 00:05:16.800
Well, the way Squirtle moves and grooves, this cliff is nothing!

99
00:05:16.866 --> 00:05:20.133
- Okay, Squirtle, ready to climb together?
- Squirtle!

100
00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:24.733
Squirtle, Squirtle, Squirtle, Squirt, Squirt, Squirt!

101
00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.633
Two, three, four!

102
00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:31.800
- One, two, one, two, one, two!
- Incredible!

103
00:05:31.866 --> 00:05:35.700
They’re good, all right, but we’ll have no problem climbing up!

104
00:05:35.766 --> 00:05:37.833
Froakie, let’s go!

105
00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:43.033
- Froakie!
- Are you ready to go up with me?

106
00:05:43.099 --> 00:05:47.133
Kie! Kie, Kie, Kie, Froak!

107
00:05:53.933 --> 00:05:57.066
- Whoa, whoa!
- Oh, no, Tierno!

108
00:05:57.133 --> 00:06:00.066
- Quick, Froakie! Use your Frubbles now!
- Froak!

109
00:06:01.833 --> 00:06:03.566
- Wow!
- Squirtle!

110
00:06:03.633 --> 00:06:07.833
- Are you okay?
- Yeah. Looks like I owe you one.

111
00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:13.333
Fro! Fro! Froakie Fro!

112
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:17.033
Way to go, Froakie! Hang on!

113
00:06:17.099 --> 00:06:19.266
- Kie!
- Awesome!

114
00:06:19.333 --> 00:06:22.166
- Thanks, Froakie.
- Froakie! Fro!

115
00:06:22.233 --> 00:06:23.833
Yippee!

116
00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:27.033
Could we stamp our card please?

117
00:06:27.099 --> 00:06:30.766
Team Froakie is the first team to get here. Here you go.

118
00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:38.366
- Fro!
- Hm!

119
00:06:38.433 --> 00:06:40.966
Let’s get to the next checkpoint! Come on!

120
00:06:43.099 --> 00:06:46.766
- See you later!
- Nothing we can do now.

121
00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:49.466
- But wait till the next time.
- Squirtle!

122
00:06:50.466 --> 00:06:53.833
Checkpoint A. The results are Team Froakie came in first

123
00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.066
and Team Squirtle came in second.

124
00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:57.966
Many thanks for the update.

125
00:07:01.833 --> 00:07:04.500
Huh? Hurry, hurry, big brother!

126
00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.866
Bulba! Saur!

127
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.000
- Fenn?
- Wait for me!

128
00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.433
Huh?

129
00:07:22.066 --> 00:07:23.066
Saur!

130
00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:25.400
-See you later!

131
00:07:25.466 --> 00:07:27.433
Oh!

132
00:07:33.599 --> 00:07:35.299
Hello! The stamp’s up here!

133
00:07:35.366 --> 00:07:37.833
I’ll go this time!

134
00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.266
- Go for it, Clemont!
- We’re counting on you!

135
00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.533
-Huh?

136
00:07:45.599 --> 00:07:47.366
-Char, Char!

137
00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:50.099
Bunnelby?

138
00:07:53.766 --> 00:07:56.700
-Char, Char! Char? Char?

139
00:07:56.766 --> 00:07:58.433
Huh?

140
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.533
Mander? Char!

141
00:08:00.599 --> 00:08:03.400
- Ah? Hm.
- Bunnel?

142
00:08:03.466 --> 00:08:05.166
Oh!

143
00:08:05.233 --> 00:08:08.900
- Well done. You’re here first!
- Huh?

144
00:08:08.966 --> 00:08:12.366
- All right! We’ve got the stamp!
- Pika!

145
00:08:18.733 --> 00:08:21.466
All the checkpoints have been cleared, Professor.

146
00:08:21.533 --> 00:08:24.433
At the present time, we’ve got Team Froakie in first place

147
00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.466
and Team Squirtle running in second place.

148
00:08:26.533 --> 00:08:29.866
As I expected, those teams are at the top.

149
00:08:29.933 --> 00:08:34.066
All that’s left now is for one to cross the finish line.

150
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.400
- We’re going to win this!
- No, we are!

151
00:08:52.066 --> 00:08:55.733
-Huh?

152
00:08:57.133 --> 00:08:59.900
- Ash, are you okay?
- Yeah.

153
00:08:59.966 --> 00:09:02.133
Maybe we should slow down.

154
00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:07.300
Huh? Oh. The fog’s so thick

155
00:09:07.366 --> 00:09:09.900
Huh? Hey, Clemont?

156
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.733
Clemont? Clemont, where are you?

157
00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.833
Pik! Pika?

158
00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:21.833
- Where’d you go? Huh?
- Na!

159
00:09:30.166 --> 00:09:33.833
- Pika? Pikachu!
- Ah!

160
00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:37.166
Pikachu, what’s going on with them?

161
00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.699
Wowee!

162
00:09:47.666 --> 00:09:51.033
- Don’t go!
- Pika! Pika!

163
00:09:53.933 --> 00:09:57.433
The fog’s everywhere. I can’t see a thing.

164
00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:00.300
Clemont, are you out there? Bonnie!

165
00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:02.266
- Wait up!
- Huh?

166
00:10:02.333 --> 00:10:04.366
I’m back here!

167
00:10:04.433 --> 00:10:07.566
- Where’s Bonnie?
- I thought she was with you.

168
00:10:07.633 --> 00:10:10.933
- Then where is she?
- Huh?

169
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.933
Huh! Hey, Pikachu’s gone, too!

170
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.466
Who’s that Pokémon?

171
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.066
It’s Charmander!

172
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.833
- This fog’s so thick!
- Yeah. You sure we’re on the right path?

173
00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.933
This is definitely the right way!

174
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.133
- There’s Ash!
- That means we’ve caught up.

175
00:10:42.199 --> 00:10:44.900
We’ll be crossing the finish line before you know it!

176
00:10:44.966 --> 00:10:46.600
Pikachu!

177
00:10:46.666 --> 00:10:49.433
- Tierno and Trevor, hold on!
- Yeah, what’s up?

178
00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.100
I’m not sure, but something doesn’t seem right.

179
00:10:52.166 --> 00:10:53.800
- Hey, Bonnie!
- Hey!

180
00:10:53.866 --> 00:10:56.699
- Ash! Is something wrong?
- Huh?

181
00:10:56.766 --> 00:11:00.900
- Have you seen Bonnie and Pikachu?
- Bonnie and Pikachu?

182
00:11:00.966 --> 00:11:03.033
Yeah. They got separated from us somehow.

183
00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.133
Wow, that’s no good. We need to search the area.

184
00:11:06.199 --> 00:11:08.500
We’ll help, if that’s okay with you.

185
00:11:08.566 --> 00:11:12.066
Thank you, but you guys should really go on with the race.

186
00:11:12.133 --> 00:11:14.133
Yeah, we don’t want to hold you back.

187
00:11:14.199 --> 00:11:16.500
How can we race when this is going on?

188
00:11:16.566 --> 00:11:18.533
Finding them is much more important than that!

189
00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:22.533
- You’d rather help us out than race?
- No contest!

190
00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.133
Thanks so much!

191
00:11:25.199 --> 00:11:27.033
Hm.

192
00:11:28.166 --> 00:11:32.033
Hey, look! I see some small footprints over there in the grass.

193
00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.000
Do you think they’re Bonnie’s?

194
00:11:34.066 --> 00:11:36.533
I think I see Pokémon footprints, too.

195
00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.933
And they look a lot like Pikachu paw prints!

196
00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.300
Really? Wow, Trevor, good job!

197
00:11:41.366 --> 00:11:45.066
Hey, I wouldn’t be surprised if Bonnie and Pikachu lost track of the path

198
00:11:45.133 --> 00:11:48.633
and wandered into the forest because the fog is so thick.

199
00:11:48.699 --> 00:11:50.466
Right! Fletchinder!

200
00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.266
Fletch!

201
00:11:53.333 --> 00:11:56.266
Fletchinder, go find Bonnie and Pikachu, okay?

202
00:11:56.333 --> 00:11:57.400
Chinder!

203
00:11:57.466 --> 00:12:00.166
Meanwhile, I think we should follow the footprints.

204
00:12:00.233 --> 00:12:02.933
Yeah, but the fog is still so thick.

205
00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.100
Don’t worry about a thing! Charmander’s flame will light the way.

206
00:12:07.166 --> 00:12:10.466
- So, Charmander, what do you say?
- Charmander!

207
00:12:19.433 --> 00:12:21.733
-Pika.

208
00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.900
Oh.

209
00:12:23.966 --> 00:12:26.133
I can’t see.

210
00:12:30.933 --> 00:12:33.600
Is this the way? Maybe.

211
00:12:33.666 --> 00:12:35.300
- Huh?
- Pika!

212
00:12:35.366 --> 00:12:37.666
-It’s a Beedrill! Run!

213
00:12:37.733 --> 00:12:41.199
- Pik, Pik, Pik!
- Oh, why did this have to happen to us?

214
00:12:41.266 --> 00:12:44.733
-Pikachu!

215
00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.833
Pika! Pika! Pika!

216
00:12:50.199 --> 00:12:53.566
- Mander!
- What’s wrong, Charmander?

217
00:12:53.633 --> 00:12:55.566
- Charmander!
- Hm!

218
00:12:57.933 --> 00:13:00.933
Hm. The footprints stop here.

219
00:13:01.933 --> 00:13:03.933
Bonnie! Pikachu!

220
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.933
-Pika, Pika, Pika, Pika!

221
00:13:09.533 --> 00:13:12.466
Oh! I hope the two of you are okay.

222
00:13:12.533 --> 00:13:14.199
- Na-na!
- Pikachu!

223
00:13:14.266 --> 00:13:16.133
-Huh?

224
00:13:18.366 --> 00:13:20.333
I’ve had enough of this!

225
00:13:23.266 --> 00:13:26.766
Na!

226
00:13:26.833 --> 00:13:30.533
I’m tired. I wonder if this is Amoonguss’s Spore.

227
00:13:33.699 --> 00:13:36.699
Oh! I’m so sleepy.

228
00:13:50.433 --> 00:13:53.199
Drifblim!

229
00:13:53.266 --> 00:13:55.000
Na! Na! Na! Na!

230
00:13:55.066 --> 00:13:58.066
- Blim! Blim! Blim! Blim!
- Loom! Loom! Loom! Loom!

231
00:13:58.133 --> 00:13:59.800
Fletch!

232
00:13:59.866 --> 00:14:02.033
Drif!

233
00:14:02.099 --> 00:14:04.666
Fletchinder!

234
00:14:04.733 --> 00:14:10.666
Fletch! Fletch! Fletch! Fletchinder!

235
00:14:10.733 --> 00:14:13.900
- Bonnie! Pikachu! Hey!
- Fletch!

236
00:14:13.966 --> 00:14:16.500
Huh? Maybe Fletchinder found them.

237
00:14:16.566 --> 00:14:18.733
- Let’s go see!
- Right!

238
00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.233
Fletchinder!

239
00:14:23.333 --> 00:14:25.933
-Squirtle!

240
00:14:28.699 --> 00:14:31.699
- Huh? Serena, what’s wrong?
- It’s an Amoonguss!

241
00:14:31.766 --> 00:14:34.066
Look out! It’s using Spore!

242
00:14:34.133 --> 00:14:36.233
Water! Spray them with water!

243
00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:39.066
- Yeah. Squirtle, Water Gun!
- Squirtle!

244
00:14:39.133 --> 00:14:42.300
Squirtle!

245
00:14:42.366 --> 00:14:43.866
Good idea!

246
00:14:43.933 --> 00:14:46.933
- Clemont, quick! Bring out Chespin!
- Huh?

247
00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:50.533
- Right!
- Froakie, I choose you!

248
00:14:50.599 --> 00:14:53.633
Now, Chespin, let’s go!

249
00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:56.666
Use Water Pulse!

250
00:14:56.733 --> 00:14:58.500
Use Pin Missile!

251
00:14:58.566 --> 00:15:00.599
Froakie!

252
00:15:00.666 --> 00:15:03.000
Chespin!

253
00:15:08.066 --> 00:15:10.233
Everything’s clearing up.

254
00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:13.400
Sorry about that, Amoonguss.

255
00:15:13.466 --> 00:15:15.300
- Fletch!
- Huh?

256
00:15:15.366 --> 00:15:16.633
Fletchinder!

257
00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:20.633
Huh?

258
00:15:22.699 --> 00:15:26.900
Wow! We would’ve gone right off that cliff if we had kept on running.

259
00:15:26.966 --> 00:15:28.466
- Pikachu!
- Huh?

260
00:15:28.533 --> 00:15:32.233
Pikachu! Oh! What happened?

261
00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:35.233
- What’s wrong?
- Pika.

262
00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.433
You're asleep!

263
00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:40.900
Hey, do you think maybe Pikachu was hit with Spore from that Amoonguss, too?

264
00:15:40.966 --> 00:15:42.966
- Maybe.
- Maybe Bonnie was, too!

265
00:15:43.033 --> 00:15:46.233
- Fletchinder! Fletch! Fletch!
- Huh?

266
00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.599
It’s trying to tell us something.

267
00:15:53.966 --> 00:15:55.699
Uh-oh. Could that be...?

268
00:15:55.766 --> 00:15:57.800
Trevor, may I look? Hm!

269
00:15:57.866 --> 00:16:02.066
- There’s no doubt about it! That’s Bonnie!
- Oh!

270
00:16:02.133 --> 00:16:03.866
But how did she end up over there?

271
00:16:03.933 --> 00:16:06.833
Don’t know, but we’ve got to get over there, too!

272
00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.900
But how do we get across this ravine?

273
00:16:08.966 --> 00:16:11.500
Clemont, why don’t you use your Aipom Arm?

274
00:16:11.566 --> 00:16:13.599
Too short! It won’t reach!

275
00:16:13.666 --> 00:16:16.333
So now what are we going to do?

276
00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:18.566
There’s just got to be a way.

277
00:16:18.633 --> 00:16:20.966
- Look at this!
- Huh?

278
00:16:21.033 --> 00:16:23.166
See?

279
00:16:24.666 --> 00:16:25.933
Drifblim!

280
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.166
A bunch of Drifblim and Drifloon.

281
00:16:28.233 --> 00:16:30.933
Maybe there’s a way we can get all of them to help us out.

282
00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:34.666
If we can figure out a way to startle them, maybe they’ll all fly up at once!

283
00:16:34.733 --> 00:16:38.099
- Then what?
- Of course! I see what you’re thinking!

284
00:16:38.166 --> 00:16:41.166
Then we can get all of them to fill in the ravine!

285
00:16:41.233 --> 00:16:45.933
We’ll use them as a bridge! The future is now, thanks to science!

286
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.133
In other words, first we’ll get them to fly up,

287
00:16:49.199 --> 00:16:53.099
then we’ll hop across them while they’re still in the ravine and rescue Bonnie!

288
00:16:53.166 --> 00:16:54.166
I get it!

289
00:16:54.233 --> 00:16:56.933
I’ll handle this. She’s my sister, after all!

290
00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.666
Hold on a minute! I’m better at this kind of stuff!

291
00:16:59.733 --> 00:17:03.466
- Let me take care of it.
- But, Ash, are you sure?

292
00:17:03.533 --> 00:17:05.266
You just get them to fly up.

293
00:17:05.333 --> 00:17:08.800
If we all work together, then rescuing Bonnie’s a cinch!

294
00:17:08.866 --> 00:17:09.966
It’s a deal!

295
00:17:14.766 --> 00:17:16.766
- Use Vine Whip!
- Chespin!

296
00:17:16.833 --> 00:17:18.666
- Use Flamethrower!
- Fennekin!

297
00:17:18.733 --> 00:17:20.700
- Use Vine Whip!
- Bulba!

298
00:17:20.766 --> 00:17:22.399
Use Water Gun!

299
00:17:22.466 --> 00:17:24.666
- Use Flamethrower!
- Char!

300
00:17:26.966 --> 00:17:31.366
- Blim! Blim! Blim! Blim!
- Loom! Loom! Loom!

301
00:17:31.433 --> 00:17:33.733
Okay, Ash! Go for it!

302
00:17:36.766 --> 00:17:40.266
- Froakie, make sure Pikachu’s okay.
- Kie!

303
00:17:42.399 --> 00:17:44.333
All right, here I go!

304
00:17:53.133 --> 00:17:54.733
Bonnie!

305
00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:56.633
Ash made it across the ravine!

306
00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.533
But that’s just the beginning. What about Bonnie?

307
00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:03.033
Bonnie! Are you okay? Huh?

308
00:18:04.399 --> 00:18:09.433
Hm. There’s only one thing to do.

309
00:18:12.766 --> 00:18:17.133
I’ve got to jump, while I still can!

310
00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.800
- Hm.
- You can do it!

311
00:18:21.866 --> 00:18:23.566
Just a little farther.

312
00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:28.666
Whoa! Whoa! Oh!

313
00:18:28.733 --> 00:18:32.733
- Fro! Fro! Fro!
- Pik. Pik. Pika.

314
00:18:34.166 --> 00:18:36.100
Pikapi!

315
00:18:38.933 --> 00:18:45.433
All or nothing!

316
00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:49.033
- Whoa!
- Pika!

317
00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.766
Pika!

318
00:19:00.733 --> 00:19:04.399
- A Pokémon you’ve never seen before?
- Yup! That’s right!

319
00:19:04.466 --> 00:19:08.666
And after it walked past me, a whole bunch of pretty flowers bloomed!

320
00:19:08.733 --> 00:19:11.666
- I couldn’t help but chase after it!
- Pikachu!

321
00:19:11.733 --> 00:19:15.666
Wow! A Pokémon that can make flowers bloom.

322
00:19:15.733 --> 00:19:19.666
Then right after that, a Beedrill... Huh?

323
00:19:19.733 --> 00:19:22.433
- Hey! There it is!
- Na-na-na!

324
00:19:26.466 --> 00:19:27.933
Wow! Hm.

325
00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.833
-Astounding!

326
00:19:29.899 --> 00:19:33.033
- Is that...
- A Pokémon? Amazing!

327
00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.600
- Yeah!
- Hm.

328
00:19:37.966 --> 00:19:39.600
I’ll check the Pokédex!

329
00:19:41.266 --> 00:19:43.200
Aw. It’s gone.

330
00:19:44.333 --> 00:19:51.166
Oh! Huh? Oh, no, I forgot to take a picture!

331
00:19:53.433 --> 00:19:57.533
Marvelous! An unexpected dead heat at the end of the race!

332
00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:00.100
Congratulations on winning your points!

333
00:20:03.166 --> 00:20:07.566
- Oh, well. No points for us.
- Pikachu!

334
00:20:07.633 --> 00:20:10.766
Hey, everybody, I’m sorry about what happened.

335
00:20:10.833 --> 00:20:12.100
I’m sorry, too.

336
00:20:12.166 --> 00:20:14.933
- Nah, don’t worry about it!
- Tierno’s right.

337
00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.800
Without what happened, we wouldn’t have seen what we just saw!

338
00:20:17.866 --> 00:20:18.866
Huh?

339
00:20:18.933 --> 00:20:22.666
And next time, I promise I’ll remember to take a picture!

340
00:20:22.733 --> 00:20:25.466
To think we saw such a mysterious Pokémon!

341
00:20:25.533 --> 00:20:29.266
- I sure hope we see it again.
- Pikachu!

342
00:20:29.333 --> 00:20:31.866
Although our heroes weren’t able to score points

343
00:20:31.933 --> 00:20:34.933
during Pokémon Orienteering on day five of camp,

344
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:40.066
they did encounter a mysterious Pokémon, a memory they will never forget!

345
00:20:40.133 --> 00:20:44.533
Soon, Professor Sycamore’s Pokémon summer camp will come to a close,

346
00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:47.000
as the journey continues!
